This affects only direct users of the lindera-dictionary crate; the lindera crate API is unchanged. The internal viterbi structs no longer expose public fields. Use the accessors instead: // v3 — direct field access
let id = word_id.id;
let cost = word_entry.word_cost; // v4 — accessors
let id = word_id.id();
let cost = word_entry.word_cost(); Other changes in lindera_dictionary::viterbi: EdgeType was removed. WordEntry gained new(), word_cost(), and word_id(); WordId gained id(). WordEntry::serialize, WordEntry::deserialize, and WordEntry::SERIALIZED_LEN are no longer public. util::read_aligned_file and the embedded_dictionary! macro were added. This list was derived from the complete machine-generated cargo public-api diff for the lindera-dictionary crate between the v3.0.7 and v4 releases.

